# Do not download a browser when installing.
#
# Nothing in backend/ drives a browser: the Playwright suites live in
# frontend/ and bring their own. This directory gets one transitively, from
# artillery -> artillery-engine-playwright -> @playwright/browser-chromium,
# whose whole purpose is a postinstall that fetches ~150MB of Chromium.
#
# That postinstall is a build dependency on Microsoft's CDN having a build for
# whatever host is installing, and on 2026-10-19 it stopped: GitHub's
# `ubuntu-latest` moved to Ubuntu 26.04, playwright-core 1.56.1 resolves that
# host to `ubuntu26.04-x64`, and no such download exists — so `npm ci` exited 1
# and took the lint, backend-test and frontend-CSP jobs with it. Bumping does
# not help; 1.59.1 maps 26.04 the same way.
#
# Read by npm for every install in this directory, which is the point: CI
# workflows, the Docker build and a developer's machine all honour it without
# each having to remember the environment variable. npm exposes it to install
# scripts as npm_config_playwright_skip_browser_download, which is where
# playwright-core's getFromENV looks after process.env.
playwright_skip_browser_download=1
